---
These defaults come from the LLMD source reviewed on 16 November 2026.

# [Batching and context length]($heading.id('batching-context-and-memory'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--batch-size=<requests>` | `16` | Limit concurrent requests in a batch. |
| `--token-batch-size=<tokens>` | `1024` | Limit the number of tokens processed in one inference step. |
| `--max-context-len=<tokens>` | `128000` | Set the server context cap. Check the model’s context length and the memory available. |
| `--prefill-chunk-size=<tokens>` | `256` | Limit the prefill chunk for each sequence. |

# [KV-cache pages and memory limits]($heading.id('kv-cache-and-memory-limits'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--page-chunk-size=<tokens>` | `16` | Set the number of tokens per KV-cache page. |
| `--gpu-memory-fraction=<fraction>` | `0.9` | Set an allocator limit on CUDA, ROCm, oneAPI, and Metal. Accepted values are greater than `0` and at most `1`. |
| `--cache-memory-fraction=<fraction>` | `0.95` | Scale the smallest reported per-device memory limit. The cache planner subtracts fixed allocations before sizing pages. Accepted values are greater than `0` and at most `1`. |

The KV cache holds attention state for tokens in active sequences. Increasing
the context limit or the number of concurrent requests can increase the cache
space needed. In the reviewed build, LFM3 uses `--data-parallel=1`. Four
sequences of 4,096 tokens each need up to 1,024 pages at 16 tokens per page.
Weights and other fixed allocations reduce the
memory available for those pages. If the cache does not fit, lower the context
or batch limit.

# [Parallel work and Decision requests]($heading.id('parallel-work-and-decision-requests'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--data-parallel=<groups>` | `1` | Set the number of groups that share request and KV-cache work in supported configurations. |
| `--systemone-window=<requests>` | Batch size divided by four, rounded down with a minimum of one | Limit the questions in flight within one [Decision request]($link.page('llmd/api-reference/decision').ref('decision')). |

The [20261106.0 release notes](https://zml.ai/posts/llmd-20261106.0/#data-parallelism-beta)
describe data parallelism on Llama as a beta feature.

# [Scheduling and attention workers]($heading.id('scheduling-and-attention-workers'))

These options are present in the reviewed source. Availability can vary by
model, backend, and release.

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--async-scheduling` | Off | Enable asynchronous scheduling on supported models. The initial beta covers Llama and Gemma 4 without speculative decoding. |
| `--attnd-workers=<count>`, `--attnd-memory=<GiB>` | Both unset | Set both to enable the attention daemon backend with the given worker count and memory budget. |
